  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "Wodɔ numekuku vovototɔ sia le Bletchley AI Safety Summit megbe, eye Yoshua Bengio kple bibimewo wu alafa ɖeka tso dukɔ blaetɔ̃ kloe kple UN, OECD kple EU la kplɔe. Egblɔ nyateƒe siwo dze le AI gãwo ƒe ŋutete kple afɔku ŋuti — egblɔ be AI ɖoɖo aɖewo va te ŋu dzesii ne wole wo dom kpɔ, eye wotrɔa woƒe nuwɔna ɖe eŋuti.",
