  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Kpɔɖeŋu si kpena ɖe sɔsrɔ̃ ŋu: HMAC-SHA256 kple nya ɣaɣla si wo katã nya, si fia laesens tokenwo siwo ku ɖe biabia ɖeka ŋu, siwo ƒe ɣeyiɣi wu enu, eye woate ŋu adzesi wo. Ele be woade asi dɔwɔnu tokenwo ŋu to mɔ evelia dzi, eye woana amegbetɔ ate ŋu akpɔ agbalẽtala ƒe ʋɔasi dukɔmetɔ le /.well-known/ te.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Woatsɔ nu enyi bubu kpe ɖe /topics ŋu, azi sia la AI dɔwɔla aɖee numekuku wo, menye asi me wotsɔ tia wo o — se ma ke tsãtɔ gale dɔ wɔm: woxɔ nuŋlɔɖi ɖe sia ɖe hedo kpe be wòle dɔ wɔm hafi woatsɔ eƒe nya aɖo, eye nyaɖeɖekpuiawo nye míawo ŋutɔ ƒe gbugbɔgbɔgblɔ. Nu wuiene le afi ma fifia.",
  "Email": "Email",
