  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "Numekuku-agbalẽwo nɔa Eŋlisigbe me gbã abe ale si wowɔ wo ene; fael siwo makina ate ŋu axlẽ la nɔa gbe aɖeke tsɔtsɔ ta o.",
  "Who is behind it": "Ame Siwo Le Eŋgɔ",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Nu si tae \"woɖe mɔ/wogbe\" ɖeka mate ŋu akpɔ AI ɣeyiɣi ƒe nuŋlɔŋlɔ zazã dzi o — kple ale si gomekpɔkpɔ akpa le be wòanɔ.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Nu Si Tae Woɖea Ʋuʋunyenye Si Womeɖo Gɔme O La Ɖa Le Hehe Dɔwɔɖoɖowo Me",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "Wilks, Ladak, kple Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) gblɔ be nunya ƒe nyaʋiʋli tso AI ƒe ɖokuisese ŋu la ŋea aɖaba ƒua susu numekuku si wowɔ tso lãwo ƒe agbenyuinɔnɔ ŋu la dzi — hoʋiʋli kple hadede ƒe dzesi ɖeka ma ke siwo léa amewo ƒe susububu tso lãwo ŋu la, woade se ɖe AI hã dzi, eɖanye AI va zu nu si le nu sem le eɖokui si gbeɖe alo mava zu o hã.",
